---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Margin Calculator – Calculate Profit Margin, Revenue & Profit"
  description="Use our margin calculator to calculate profit margin, profit, revenue, or cost. Easily find selling price and gross margin from your business numbers."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="Margin Calculator"
  slug="margin-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'margin calculator',
    'profit margin calculator',
    'gross margin calculator',
    'gross profit calculator',
    'sales margin calculator',
    'profit calculator',
    'gross margin formula',
    'profit margin formula',
    'margin vs markup',
    'selling price calculator',
    'cogs calculator'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- CALCULATION MODE SELECTOR TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-3 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 hidden md:inline">
          Calculation Mode:
        </span>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-1.5 w-full md:w-auto text-xs font-bold">
          <button type="button" class="btn-margin-mode active rounded-xl border border-blue-600 bg-blue-50 px-3 py-2 text-blue-700 dark:border-blue-500 dark:bg-blue-950/60 dark:text-blue-300 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="cost_margin">
            🏷️ Cost + Margin
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-margin-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="cost_revenue">
            💰 Cost + Revenue
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-margin-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="revenue_margin">
            🔄 Revenue + Margin
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-margin-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="revenue_profit">
            📈 Revenue + Profit
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-margin-mode rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-2 text-slate-700 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 hover:border-slate-400 transition cursor-pointer text-center" data-mode="cost_profit">
            ⚖️ Cost + Profit
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
        <div>
          <h2 id="txt-margin-panel-title" class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>📈</span> Margin &amp; Selling Price Calculator
          </h2>
          <p id="txt-margin-subtitle" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Calculate your required selling price and profit from cost of goods sold (COGS) and desired profit margin.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Currency Selector -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 shrink-0 text-xs">
          <label for="sel-currency" class="font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">Currency:</label>
          <select id="sel-currency" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-2.5 py-1.5 font-bold text-slate-800 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
            <option value="₹" selected>₹ INR (Rupee)</option>
            <option value="$">$ USD (Dollar)</option>
            <option value="€">€ EUR (Euro)</option>
            <option value="£">£ GBP (Pound)</option>
            <option value="¥">¥ JPY (Yen)</option>
          </select>
        </div>
      </div>

      <form id="form-margin" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <!-- SECTION: DYNAMIC INPUT FIELDS ACCORDING TO MODE -->

        <!-- Mode 1: Cost + Desired Margin -->
        <div id="sec-mode-cost-margin" class="space-y-4">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-cm-cost" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Cost of Goods Sold / COGS (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cm-cost" value="30" step="0.5" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 30" />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Direct material, labor, or wholesale purchase cost.</span>
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-cm-margin" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Desired Profit Margin (%)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cm-margin" value="40" step="0.5" min="0" max="99.99" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 40" />
              <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Target percentage of final selling price (must be &lt; 100%).</span>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- Quick Margin Presets -->
          <div class="pt-2 border-t border-slate-100 dark:border-slate-800">
            <span class="block text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-1.5">Quick Margin Presets:</span>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-1.5">
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="10">10%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="15">15%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="20">20%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="25">25%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="30">30%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="40">40%</button>
              <button type="button" class="btn-quick-margin rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 px-2.5 py-1 text-xs font-bold hover:bg-blue-50 hover:text-blue-600 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-300 cursor-pointer" data-margin="50">50%</button>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mode 2: Cost + Selling Price / Revenue -->
        <div id="sec-mode-cost-revenue" class="hidden space-y-4">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-cr-cost" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Cost of Goods Sold / COGS (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cr-cost" value="30" step="0.5" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 30" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-cr-rev" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Selling Price / Total Revenue (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cr-rev" value="50" step="0.5" min="0.01" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 50" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mode 3: Revenue + Margin -->
        <div id="sec-mode-revenue-margin" class="hidden space-y-4">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-rm-rev" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Selling Price / Target Revenue (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-rm-rev" value="100" step="0.5" min="0.01" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 100" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-rm-margin" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Profit Margin Target (%)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-rm-margin" value="25" step="0.5" min="0" max="99.99" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 25" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mode 4: Revenue + Profit -->
        <div id="sec-mode-revenue-profit" class="hidden space-y-4">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-rp-rev" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Selling Price / Total Revenue (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-rp-rev" value="200" step="0.5" min="0.01" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 200" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-rp-profit" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Target Gross Profit (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-rp-profit" value="50" step="0.5" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 50" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Mode 5: Cost + Profit -->
        <div id="sec-mode-cost-profit" class="hidden space-y-4">
          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-cp-cost" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Cost of Goods Sold / COGS (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cp-cost" value="100" step="0.5" min="0" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 100" />
            </div>

            <div>
              <label for="inp-cp-profit" class="block text-xs font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
                Desired Gross Profit (<span class="txt-cur-symbol">₹</span>)
              </label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-cp-profit" value="50" step="0.5" class="mt-1 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="e.g. 50" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- ACTION BUTTONS -->
        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-margin" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate Margin &amp; Price →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-margin" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer" title="Reset fields">
            Reset (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <!-- ACCESSIBLE ERROR -->
        <p id="err-margin" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION -->
      <div id="margin-results-section" class="mt-6 space-y-6">
        
        <!-- 1. MAIN RESULT HERO CARD -->
        <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-blue-50/40 to-blue-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-blue-500/5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-blue-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-blue-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span id="lbl-hero-title" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
                REQUIRED SELLING PRICE
              </span>
              <div id="res-hero-amount" class="mt-1 text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-5xl font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
                ₹ 50.00
              </div>
              <div id="res-hero-subtitle" class="text-xs font-semibold text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mt-0.5">
                Yields 40.00% Gross Profit Margin
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Gross Profit:</span>
              <div id="res-hero-secondary" class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
                ₹ 20.00
              </div>
              <div id="res-hero-markup-badge" class="text-xs font-bold text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300 mt-0.5">
                Markup: 66.67%
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <!-- 5-Box Key Financial Metrics Summary -->
          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 lg:grid-cols-5 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Cost (COGS)</div>
              <div id="res-grid-cost" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 30.00</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Selling Price</div>
              <div id="res-grid-rev" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">₹ 50.00</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Gross Profit</div>
              <div id="res-grid-profit" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 20.00</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Profit Margin</div>
              <div id="res-grid-margin" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-purple-600 dark:text-purple-400">40.00%</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-blue-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70 col-span-2 sm:col-span-1">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Equivalent Markup</div>
              <div id="res-grid-markup" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">66.67%</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. STEP-BY-STEP CALCULATION BREAKDOWN -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-2 border-b border-slate-200 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📐</span> Step-by-Step Calculation Breakdown
            </h3>
            <span class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-mono" id="txt-breakdown-title">
              Selling Price from Cost &amp; Margin
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40 space-y-2 text-xs font-mono">
            <div class="text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
              Formula: <strong id="txt-breakdown-formula" class="text-slate-900 dark:text-white font-mono">Revenue = Cost ÷ (1 - Margin ÷ 100)</strong>
            </div>
            <div id="box-breakdown-steps" class="pt-1 border-t border-slate-200/80 dark:border-slate-800 space-y-1.5">
              <!-- Steps injected dynamically -->
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. MARGIN COMPARISON TABLE & PDF DOWNLOAD -->
        <div class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-2">
            <div>
              <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span>📊</span> Margin &amp; Markup Comparison Matrix
              </h3>
              <p class="text-[11px] text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">
                Compare selling price, profit, and markup across common margin percentages for your cost.
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- Download PDF Button -->
            <button type="button" id="btn-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-xl bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3.5 py-1.5 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download calculation as PDF">
              <span>📄</span> <span>Download PDF</span>
            </button>
          </div>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-2.5 rounded-l-lg">Target Margin</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right">Selling Price</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right">Gross Profit</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right rounded-r-lg font-bold text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400">Equivalent Markup</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="tbl-comparison" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Rows injected dynamically -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL CONTENT SLOT -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="margin-content">
      
      <h2>What is Profit Margin?</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Profit margin</strong> is a fundamental financial metric that measures the proportion of revenue that remains as profit after deducting the associated costs of producing or acquiring goods and services. Expressed as a percentage, it reveals how many cents of profit a business retains for every dollar or rupee generated in sales.
      </p>
      <p>
        In everyday commerce and retail, the term most frequently refers to <strong>gross profit margin</strong>, which assesses the direct relationship between your <strong>Cost of Goods Sold (COGS)</strong> and your retail selling price before factoring in fixed administrative expenses, rent, or financing obligations.
      </p>

      <h2>How to Calculate Profit Margin Step-by-Step</h2>
      <p>
        Calculating profit margin requires four straightforward steps:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>Determine your Cost of Goods Sold (COGS):</strong> Identify the direct production, wholesale purchase, or acquisition cost per unit.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Determine your Selling Price / Revenue:</strong> Establish the final price charged to the customer.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Calculate Gross Profit:</strong> Subtract the cost from the selling price:
          <br />
          <code>Gross Profit = Revenue - Cost</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Divide Profit by Revenue and Multiply by 100:</strong>
          <br />
          <code>Profit Margin (%) = (Profit / Revenue) × 100</code>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 p-4 dark:border-blue-900/50 dark:bg-blue-950/30">
        <h4 class="font-bold text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-200 text-sm mb-1">Practical Step-by-Step Example</h4>
        <p class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          Suppose an apparel retailer purchases a jacket for <strong>₹30</strong> (Cost) and sells it for <strong>₹50</strong> (Revenue):
        </p>
        <ul class="text-xs text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 mt-2 space-y-1">
          <li><strong>Step 1 (Profit):</strong> ₹50 - ₹30 = <strong>₹20 profit</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 2 (Margin Ratio):</strong> ₹20 ÷ ₹50 = <strong>0.40</strong>.</li>
          <li><strong>Step 3 (Percentage):</strong> 0.40 × 100 = <strong>40% profit margin</strong>.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <h2>Gross Margin Formula</h2>
      <p>
        The mathematical formula for calculating gross profit margin is:
      </p>
      <pre><code>Gross Margin (%) = ((Revenue - COGS) / Revenue) × 100</code></pre>
      <p>
        Because <code>Profit = Revenue - COGS</code>, the formula can also be written succinctly as:
      </p>
      <pre><code>Profit Margin (%) = (Profit / Revenue) × 100</code></pre>

      <h2>How to Calculate Selling Price for a Desired Margin</h2>
      <p>
        The most common business challenge is knowing your product cost and wanting to price it so you achieve a specific profit margin. 
        Many people make the critical mistake of simply multiplying the cost by the margin percentage (e.g. adding 40% to ₹30 gives ₹42, but ₹12 profit on ₹42 is only a 28.57% margin, not 40%).
      </p>
      <p>
        To hit your target margin accurately, use the <strong>selling price formula</strong>:
      </p>
      <pre><code>Selling Price = Cost / (1 - Desired Margin / 100)</code></pre>
      <p>
        <strong>Worked Example:</strong> If your product costs <strong>₹30</strong> and your target margin is <strong>40%</strong>:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li>Convert margin percentage to a decimal: <code>40 ÷ 100 = 0.40</code>.</li>
        <li>Subtract from 1: <code>1 - 0.40 = 0.60</code>.</li>
        <li>Divide cost by 0.60: <code>₹30 ÷ 0.60 = ₹50.00</code>.</li>
        <li>Verify: Selling at ₹50 gives ₹20 profit, and <code>(₹20 ÷ ₹50) × 100 = 40%</code> exactly.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Margin vs Markup: The Crucial Distinction</h2>
      <p>
        While both terms describe the relationship between cost, profit, and selling price, they measure completely different percentages:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Margin</strong> is calculated as a percentage of the <em>selling price</em>:
          <br />
          <code>Margin (%) = (Profit / Selling Price) × 100</code>
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Markup</strong> is calculated as a percentage of the <em>cost</em>:
          <br />
          <code>Markup (%) = (Profit / Cost) × 100</code>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <div class="overflow-x-auto my-4">
        <table class="w-full text-left text-xs border border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800">
          <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 font-bold">
            <tr>
              <th class="p-2.5">Metric</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Cost</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Selling Price</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Profit</th>
              <th class="p-2.5">Calculation Formula</th>
              <th class="p-2.5 text-right font-black">Resulting Rate</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-slate-200 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
            <tr>
              <td class="p-2.5 font-bold font-sans">Margin</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹100</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹150</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹50</td>
              <td class="p-2.5 font-sans">(₹50 ÷ ₹150) × 100</td>
              <td class="p-2.5 text-right font-bold text-blue-600">33.33%</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-2.5 font-bold font-sans">Markup</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹100</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹150</td>
              <td class="p-2.5">₹50</td>
              <td class="p-2.5 font-sans">(₹50 ÷ ₹100) × 100</td>
              <td class="p-2.5 text-right font-bold text-amber-600">50.00%</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <p>
        Notice that markup is always higher than margin for the same dollar profit. Confusing the two can lead to severe underpricing and lost revenue.
      </p>

      <h2>Gross Profit vs Net Profit Margin</h2>
      <p>
        It is essential to understand the difference between gross margin and net margin when evaluating your business health:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Gross Profit Margin:</strong> Focuses exclusively on revenue after subtracting direct product manufacturing, labor, or procurement costs (COGS). It reflects pricing power and direct production efficiency.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Net Profit Margin:</strong> The ultimate "bottom line" measure. It deducts all business expenditures from revenue, including rent, employee salaries, software subscriptions, logistics, corporate income taxes, and debt interest.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        <em>Note:</em> This calculator is specifically designed for <strong>gross profit margin</strong> calculations based on unit costs and sales revenues. For full financial accounting, operating overhead must be evaluated across your overall profit and loss statement.
      </p>

      <h2>What is a Good Profit Margin?</h2>
      <p>
        There is no single universal percentage that defines a "good" margin. What constitutes a healthy profit margin depends heavily on the industry, business model, operating overhead, and sales turnover velocity:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Supermarkets &amp; Grocery Retail (2%–5% Net Margin):</strong> Extremely tight margins are balanced by massive sales volume and rapid inventory turnover.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>General Retail &amp; E-Commerce (10%–25% Gross Margin):</strong> Standard consumer goods typically aim for healthy gross margins to cover advertising and fulfillment costs.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Manufacturing &amp; Engineering (25%–35% Gross Margin):</strong> Balances raw material pricing and equipment depreciation.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Software &amp; SaaS (70%–85% Gross Margin):</strong> Near-zero marginal distribution costs yield exceptionally high gross margins, though substantial R&amp;D and sales overhead must be covered.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Professional Services &amp; Consulting (30%–50% Margin):</strong> High margins offset by direct expert labor costs and talent retention.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        A high gross margin does not automatically guarantee overall business profitability if your customer acquisition and operating expenses remain excessive.
      </p>

      <h2>Related Financial Calculators</h2>
      <p>
        Optimize your business pricing and tax compliance with our related financial utilities:
